<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Mary's Church, Lübeck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1250–1350</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Marienkirche, Lübeck</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Mary's Church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> is a brick Gothic church built by the city's merchants between about 1250 and 1350 beside the town hall. Its soaring nave became the model for many churches around the Baltic and expressed the wealth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>. Badly damaged in a bombing raid in 1942, it has since been restored.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-marys-church-lubeck.jpg" alt="St. Mary's Church, Lübeck" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carsten Steger · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_image_of_St._Mary%27s_Church,_L%C3%BCbeck_(view_from_the_west).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
